    "result_text": "All 26 tests pass, including the ones covering the new behavior (Cp09 per-city sequence, Cp14 membership number, Cp16 city-prefix format).\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 reworked `nextCustomerCode`:\n- Now takes the owner's `city` in addition to `lastName`.\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city (via `Math.min(3, \u2026)` for short cities).\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name (unchanged).\n- `NNNN` = a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence \u2014 one more than the number of owners already registered in that city, using the existing `householdKey` normalization (trim/collapse/lowercase) for case-insensitive city matching, instead of the old global owner count.\n- Updated the call site to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 `getMembershipNumber()` already builds `<customerCode>-M<YY>` generically, so it automatically inherits the new format; I only updated its javadoc example (`SMI-0007-M26` \u2192 `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`) to match. Every value derived from `customerCode` (membership number) is now rebuilt on the new format automatically.",
